<div style="max-width:580px;margin:24px 0"><h3 style="font-size:24px;line-height:30px;font-weight:700">Deep Dive: Why the Bean Market Is Tight</h3>
<p>In one valley, a family farm that has grown coffee for generations is <a href="https://news.example.org/REDACTED" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Farm Faces Hard Choices" target="_blank">weighing its future after a poor harvest</a>.</p>
<ul style="margin-top:24px;padding-inline-start:24px">
<li style="font-weight:400"><strong>In the north</strong>, growers are calling on officials to act over rising costs.</li>
<li style="font-weight:400"><strong>Across the region</strong>, buyers are paying more for beans after two weak seasons.</li>
<li style="font-weight:400"><strong>Shipping rates</strong> have climbed sharply; <a href="https://news.example.org/REDACTED" rel="noopener noreferrer" title="Freight Costs Climb" target="_blank">freight costs hit a record</a> last week.</li>
<li style="font-weight:400"><strong>With an election</strong> coming, the issue is moving up the agenda.</li></ul></div>
